    "q-37221": {
      "dom_id": "step-q37221",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227500/assets/bbe19cf01b4ca415802db1d505b402e2c238aad6c443170cf18cd7b79d7f238a.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the points shown are the local maxima of the function?",
      "worked_solution": "Consider the point $Q.$ We can take an open interval of $x$-values such that $Q$ will be the highest point on the graph in this interval. Hence, $Q$ is a local maximum.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227500/assets/14d2e4c17f5a79165c2e6b1988fe949625eccb87d2880b1131705028be5884c4.png)",
