    "q-108296": {
      "dom_id": "step-q108296",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227500/assets/e0b8b8968b650e53d35766ede2b22aa187a7301f559d1687fa6bc630c1152701.png)\n\nThe graph of a function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $f(x)$ attains a local minimum at $x=-2$\n\nII. $f(x)$ attains a **global** minimum at $x=1$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ attains a local maximum at $x=3$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function has a local minimum at $x=-2.$ For example, in the interval $(-2.5,-1.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=-2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227500/assets/f7abc15ac37d26d6daea9855cdebd2ef0ae5e27a27d65480b51da3cb7b19a395.png)\n\n \nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\ge f(-2)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (-2.5,-1.5).$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the function has a global minimum at $x=1.$ The global minimum is the lowest point on the graph and our function does not have points where its value is smaller than $f(1).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function has a local maximum at $x=3.$ For example, in the interval $(2.5,3.5),$ the greatest value of the function is attained at $x=3,$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227500/assets/19d3370f7113e6ebfaa2d1f53a3d097de796e6d3413f06414d35e6a7ade9b9b6.png)\n\n \nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\le f(3)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (2.5,3.5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
